message.content:
This looks like a CBP ruling on synthetic sea salt for reef aquariums. I recall that mixtures of salts like this are classified in heading 3824 (chemical products and preparations, not elsewhere specified), though some rulings put them in 2501 (salt). Heading 2501 covers sodium chloride, pure or not, including sea water. A mixture of several different salts, though, falls outside the chapter 25 and chapter 28 headings, since chapter 28 and 25 cover only separate defined compounds, so a deliberate mixture goes to 3824.

Within 3824, the residual subheading 3824.99 applies. The statistical suffix I remember for "other" is 3824.99.9295 (older 3824.90.9290), but I'm unsure of it. Under the current schedule, 3824.99.92 is "Other" under "Other: Other", and its 10-digit statistical suffixes are 3824.99.9285, 3824.99.9290 and 3824.99.9295 in some versions. I'll go with 3824.99.9295.

{"hts_code": "3824.99.9295", "reason": "A deliberately formulated mixture of several salts (NaCl, sulfates, chlorides) is not a single defined compound or plain salt of chapters 25/28, so it falls in the residual chemical preparations heading 3824, other."}
